## The problem

People add a plant and then nothing happens. Of the 418 plants added in the last 30 days, I cannot say how
many got a first reminder, because a reminder leaves no record — the worker reads a date off the plant and
sends an email with its own text. The people I asked say they "got one at some point" or "never got one".
The product's whole promise is the reminder, and I cannot see whether it is kept.

## Evidence

Run again before quoting; the numbers were read 2026-10-01.

| What | Query | Read 2026-10-01 |
|---|---|---|
| plants added, last 30 days | `select count(*) from plants where created_at > now() - interval '30 days'` | 418 |
| reminders recorded | `select count(*) from reminders` | **the table does not exist** |
| people with ≥ 1 plant and no watering logged in 14 days | `select count(distinct user_id) from plants p where not exists (select 1 from waterings w where w.plant_id = p.id and w.at > now() - interval '14 days')` | 131 of 212 |

## Success metric

`plant_added → first_reminder_delivered` within 24 hours, for people adding their first plant. The last
event in the chain is **delivered** — whoever sends is on the critical path.

## Non-goals

- Browser push notifications (open as D-1; not in this item).
- Snoozing, "water all", or more than one plant per reminder.
- Changing how often a plant drinks — the default schedule stays.

## Who is affected

Everyone who adds a plant. Today 212 people; all have a verified email address.

## Verdict gates

Each is taken once, on the date it names, and never retried for a better number.

- **🚦-1** — Of the people who add their **first** plant in the week after release, **≥ 60 %** receive a
  first reminder within 24 hours. Measured from the `reminders` table: rows with `sent_at` not null and
  `sent_at - plant.created_at ≤ 24 h`, over first plants created in that week.
- **🚦-2** — Of first reminders delivered in that week, **≥ 30 %** are acted on within 48 hours
  (`reminder_acted` recorded with the reminder's id).
- **🚦-3** — **Zero** reminders sent for a plant deleted before the reminder's due time, over the same
  week: `select count(*) from reminders r join plants p on p.id = r.plant_id where p.deleted_at < r.due_at and r.sent_at is not null`.
